%% Two-tap line lifecycle state diagram
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Idle

  state "Idle / no pending line" as Idle
  note right of Idle
    No pending start, line preview, line commit intent,
    or pointer-owned line overlay exists.
  end note

  Idle --> FirstTapGate: finite first tap in line tool
  Idle --> Idle: non-line tool, invalid tap, or stale sample / ignore
  Idle --> Disposed: runtime.dispose()

  state "First tap admission" as FirstTapGate
  note right of FirstTapGate
    The first tap stores finite start facts, current tool,
    and current document/controller epoch. It never creates
    a line element, commit intent, action, or document signal.
  end note

  FirstTapGate --> PendingStart: start finite and tool style drawable / store pending start, publish overlay pending marker
  FirstTapGate --> Idle: non-finite start, non-drawable style, or inactive surface / no commit
  FirstTapGate --> Disposed: disposed runtime / StateError

  state "Pending start / epoch-bound" as PendingStart
  note right of PendingStart
    Pending line state outlives unrelated pointer-session
    terminal cleanup. Only line-owned cleanup, mode/tool
    change, successful load, cancel, dispose, or terminal
    line decision may clear it.
  end note

  PendingStart --> LinePreview: finite pointer move with same tool and epoch / overlay line preview only
  PendingStart --> SecondTapGate: finite second tap
  PendingStart --> CleanupOnly: cancel, mode/tool change, or loadDocument success
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: loadDocument failure / preserve pending start and preview
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: interactive=false / disable future routing only; preserve pending start
  PendingStart --> PendingStart: unrelated pointer cleanup or stale non-terminal sample / preserve pending start
  PendingStart --> DisposeCleanup: runtime.dispose()

  state "Line preview / overlay only" as LinePreview
  note right of LinePreview
    Preview facts are immutable overlay state. No selected-move
    main-scene preview, resolver call, Store mutation, spatial
    update, projection eviction, action, or document notification
    is allowed while previewing.
  end note

  LinePreview --> LinePreview: finite move with same tool and epoch / replace overlay preview end
  LinePreview --> SecondTapGate: finite second tap
  LinePreview --> CleanupOnly: cancel, mode/tool change, or loadDocument success
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: loadDocument failure / preserve pending line
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: interactive=false / disable future routing only; preserve line preview
  LinePreview --> LinePreview: unrelated pointer cleanup or stale non-terminal sample / preserve preview
  LinePreview --> DisposeCleanup: runtime.dispose()

  state "Second tap terminal gate" as SecondTapGate
  note right of SecondTapGate
    A terminal tap may create a commit intent only when the
    pending start still exists, tool and epoch match, start/end
    are finite, and style facts remain valid.
  end note

  SecondTapGate --> CleanupOnly: no pending start, stale epoch, tool mismatch, invalid terminal, or non-finite facts
  SecondTapGate --> CommitIntent: same tool and epoch with finite start/end and valid style facts

  state "Commit intent / EditKernel only" as CommitIntent
  note right of CommitIntent
    InteractionEngine submits a synchronous EditKernel request
    to add the line. It does not mutate DocumentStoreKernel
    directly and does not publish drawLine before commit success.
  end note

  CommitIntent --> EditKernelOutcome: open interaction edit and stage drawLine action descriptor

  state "EditKernel outcome" as EditKernelOutcome
  note right of EditKernelOutcome
    Atomic install is the only commit boundary. Rollback,
    rejected Future, stale handle, preflight failure, or exception
    leaves committed document revisions, spatial index,
    projection cache, main repaint, and drawLine action unchanged.
  end note

  EditKernelOutcome --> SuccessfulCommit: atomic install accepted
  EditKernelOutcome --> CleanupOnly: rollback, rejection, preflight failure, or exception

  state "Successful commit installed" as SuccessfulCommit
  SuccessfulCommit --> CleanupAfterCommit: close edit session and mark pending line cleared

  state "Cleanup after successful commit" as CleanupAfterCommit
  note right of CleanupAfterCommit
    Pending start and overlay preview are cleared before public
    document/action/repaint signals are observed.
  end note

  CleanupAfterCommit --> PublishCommitSignals: pending line and preview cleared

  state "Publish successful commit signals" as PublishCommitSignals
  note right of PublishCommitSignals
    Publish document revision notification, drawLine action,
    main repaint for the committed line, and overlay cleanup
    repaint only after the successful EditKernel outcome.
  end note
  PublishCommitSignals --> Idle: signals published

  state "Cleanup only / no committed effects" as CleanupOnly
  note left of CleanupOnly
    Clears pending start and line overlay preview only. No line
    element, document notification, drawLine action, spatial delta,
    projection eviction, or main-scene preview is produced.
    overlayRevision advances only when pending preview was visible.
  end note
  CleanupOnly --> OverlayCleanup: pending overlay was visible
  CleanupOnly --> Idle: no visible overlay

  state "Overlay cleanup repaint" as OverlayCleanup
  OverlayCleanup --> Idle: overlay cleanup published

  state "Dispose cleanup" as DisposeCleanup
  note left of DisposeCleanup
    Runtime disposal clears pending line and preview before
    streams close. Later samples cannot revive or commit it.
  end note
  DisposeCleanup --> Disposed: pending line cleared

  state "Disposed runtime" as Disposed
  Disposed --> Disposed: later pointer/edit operation / StateError
  Disposed --> Disposed: dispose() again / no side effects

  note left of CommitIntent
    Negative invariants:
    no selected-move resolver;
    no selected-move main-scene preview;
    no direct Store mutation;
    no legacy source as normative architecture.
  end note
